@startuml 17-seq-web-push
!include ../../_style.iuml
title Nós no Cabo v1 — Web Push for submitters who left

actor Submitter
participant "SPA\nusePushSubscription" as spa
participant "sw.js" as sw
participant "catalog" as catalog
database "catalog D1" as db
participant "Push service" as push <<external>>
participant "cron\n41 * * * *" as cron <<cron>>

== Subscribe ==
Submitter -> spa : grants notification permission\n(bell on a draft card)
spa -> sw : register /sw.js
spa -> push : pushManager.subscribe(VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY)
loop each checking draft, once
  spa -> catalog : POST /v1/websites/:id/subscriptions\n(PushSubscription.toJSON())
  catalog -> db : insert push_subscriptions\n(only while checking, ≤ 5 per site,\nknown push service endpoints only)
  catalog --> spa : 204
end

== Decision ==
alt moderation (applyModeration) or an email review reply
  catalog -> db : claim subscriptions of the site
else review script (writes D1 directly)
  cron -> catalog : sweepPushes
  catalog -> db : claim subscriptions of decided sites;\ndelete those older than 7 days
end
catalog -> push : RFC 8291 encrypted payload,\nRFC 8292 VAPID JWT (WebCrypto)
note right: best effort: a claimed subscription is\ndeleted even if its push fails
push -> sw : push event
sw -> Submitter : notification "{name} foi publicado"\nor "{name} não foi aceito"
Submitter -> sw : click
sw -> spa : openWindow(/website/:id or /websites)

note over spa
  Off while MSW mocks are on (MSW owns the root scope)
  or without VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY. In-tab status
  checks stay as the fallback. No VAPID keys = no sending.
end note

@enduml
